Here's the hidden truth behind every modern database:
 • Disk I/O dominates latency, not CPU.
 • B-Trees minimize reads by packing keys + pointers into page-sized nodes.
 • Fan-out makes them shallow, keeping most lookups within 2–3 page reads.
 • Concurrency + buffer pools turn them into the workhorse of indexing.

This isn't theory, it's why PostgreSQL, MySQL, and SQLite all default to B-Trees.

